# Run payloads: frames are large and regenerable from the ledger, which is not.
# The ledger, the books, the snapshots, the probes, the surprises, the desk
# transcripts and the manifest ARE tracked -- they are the account.
runs/*/trace.jsonl
runs/dryrun-*/
runs/pytest-*/
runs/smoke*/
runs_live.log
.live_slug
__pycache__/
*.pyc

.pytest_cache/

# One leg's candidate stream is 201 MB -- 19 486 candidates averaging 10 KB
# each, from 20260729T004020Z-leg01. GitHub refuses anything over 100 MB, so
# this file cannot be pushed and the branch carrying it cannot either.
#
# Excluded by path rather than by a blanket `runs/*/candidates.jsonl`, because
# the stream is normally worth tracking and eighteen of them already are (the
# next largest is 18.8 MB). The size is the anomaly, not the artefact: a
# 10 KB mean candidate is a signal about what the miner is emitting, and it is
# filed as such rather than being quietly dropped here.
runs/20260729T004020Z-leg01/candidates.jsonl
